From 9e587585d0237929349275b7cbbbf12f4470f608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:20:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi: start the audio DSP (ADSP), Q6 core ready over APR

sweet_slpi.c takes the remote processor as parameters (host, IPCC client,
SMP2P items, PAS id, region, log tag, boot-arg prefix); sweet_adsp.c compiles
it again for the ADSP (pas 1, region 0x8bb00000, host 2, IPCC client 3, SMP2P
443/429) with an "apr_audio_svc" channel instead of FastRPC. On that channel
it asks the Q6 core for its state (AVCS_CMD_ADSP_EVENT_GET_STATE) and then
the service versions.

Loader fixes found on the way: segments are streamed from the file through a
16 KiB buffer (kfree_data of the ADSP's 11 MB segment buffer panicked in
vm_map_delete on a permanent entry), and both DSPs share one set of device
mappings (the ADSP's second 2 MiB ml_io_map of SMEM found no I/O space).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
